+| SCENARIO-KAN-5291 | Low-Order Curriculum Reports Order, Slack, And False Controls | Implemented-Partial | Artifact follows the bounded CPU measurement path using Exp 5277 and Exp 5278 fixtures, reports factor-order metrics, certificate success by order, false-property rejection, slack, solve time, piece counts, and failure classes, and certifies all curriculum and shuffled stages; however, success_advantage_over_shuffled=0.0 and honest_verdict.value says the low-order curriculum did not improve certificate success over shuffled ordering, so this remains a measurement research finding rather than an implemented curriculum-improvement win. |
